From: Recalbox <build@recalbox.com>
Date: Sun, 03 May 2026 18:24:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] guncon2: 31kHz/15kHz support + adaptive cache + modeline-aware reset

GunCon 2 driver tuned for the RGB Dual board (15kHz and 31kHz outputs)
and for the retroarch lightgun stack:

- Y 16-bit decode + sticky 8/16-bit detection, scaled to [0..480].
  Always *2 in 8-bit Y mode (regardless of screen height): the old
  condition 'screen_height > 240' left Y stuck in upper half in 240p.
- Per-axis lazy cache + sentinel filtering (X=0/Y=5)
- Off-screen detection: x_invalid_streak > 8 (~64ms) clears last_x to 0.
- No hold_lock bump on rising edge: retroarch handles the post-flash
  window itself (POSITION_LOCKED + adaptive deliver window).
- mode_flags=0x0100 forced via SET_REPORT (shared 15kHz and 31kHz).
- Drop USB soft-reset on open(): saves ~150ms latency at retroarch
  launch. The firmware keeps mode_flags=0x0100 across sessions; we
  still re-send the SET_REPORT and re-submit the URB.
- Auto-cal linear X mapping with modeline-change reset: when the fb
  'modes' string changes (15kHz <-> 31kHz, progressive <-> interlaced,
  refresh, ...), the firmware's raw X plage shifts. We reset
  x_auto_min/max + y_is_8bit so the new mode rebuilds bounds.

Signed-off-by: Recalbox <build@recalbox.com>
---
